 "source_url": "https://www.instagram.com/reel/De1Iy5KB-_s/",
 "title": "Three Ways to Tell Better Stories in Content",
 "topic": "content creation",
 "summary": "The creator explains three techniques to improve storytelling in content by getting specific, raising the stakes, and connecting events through conflict and consequences. She demonstrates this by showing examples of bad, OK, and great storytelling based on missing a train.",
 "key_points": [
  "Get specific: Add little details that put the audience in the moment, such as what you saw, heard, felt, smelt, or tasted.",
  "Raise the stakes: Show what you wanted and what you stood to lose.",
  "Connect events through conflict and consequences: Explain what got in the way and how you overcame obstacles.",
  "Bad storytelling example: I missed the train this morning, so then I missed my meeting.",
  "OK storytelling example: I missed my train by 10 seconds, so then I missed out on a meeting with a dream client.",
  "Great storytelling example: The doors literally shut with my hands on them and I watched my train take off without me. My meeting was in 22 minutes and the next train was in 20, so I knew that I was screwed."
 ],
 "content": "Three ways to tell better stories in content: 1. Get specific. Add little details that put us in the moment - what you saw/ heard/felt/smelt/tasted 2. Raise the stakes - What did you want/ what do you stand to lose? 3. Connect events through conflict and consequences. What got in the way, how did you overcome obstacles? Make a note of this post. I missed the train this morning, so then I missed my meeting. I missed my train by 10 seconds, so then I missed out on a meeting with a dream client. The doors literally shut with my hands on them and I watched my train take off without me. My meeting was in 22 minutes and the next train was in 20, so I knew that I was screwed.",
